   "id": 505981,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Calculate <span data-math=\"4.5 \\times {10^3} + 9.8 \\times {10^2}\">4.5 \\times {10^3} + 9.8 \\times {10^2}</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"4.5 \\times {10^3} + 9.8 \\times {10^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>First, you need to make the powers of 10 match.</p>\n<p>Make them both have an exponent of 3. Move the decimal point one place to the left on the second number.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0.98 \\times {10^3}\"></span></p>\n<p>Because the powers of 10 match, use the distributive property to factor the power of 10 from the numbers. Then, add the other part of the numbers separately.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"4.5 \\times {10^3} + 0.98 \\times {10^3}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(4.5 + 0.98) \\times {10^3}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"5.48 \\times {10^3}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"5.48 \\times {10^3}\">5.48 \\times {10^3}</span>"
    }
   ],
